Plato, Republic 353e: ἆρ᾽ οὖν ἔστιν ψυχῆς ἀρετή;
'Is there, then, an excellence of the soul?' ἀρετή is nominative singular; ψυχῆς is genitive singular of ψυχή (soul).

The first declension feminine in -η is the home of abstract nouns and of many common words: τέχνη (art, skill), τιμή (honor), ἀλήθεια (truth), δίκη (justice).
